// boxcxx — <__bits/ranges_algo_sort>
// Ф29b-2, second file: the ranges:: constrained PARTITIONING ([alg.partitions]),
// SORTING ([alg.sort]), HEAP ([alg.heap.operations]) and PERMUTATION-generator
// ([alg.permutation.generators]) niebloids. Pulled in by <algorithm> after
// <__bits/ranges_algo_mut>.
//
// The heavy reordering engines already live, tested, in <algorithm> (introsort
// `sort`, merge-based `stable_sort`, quickselect `nth_element`, the heap
// primitives, `stable_partition`, the permutation generators). Rather than
// duplicate several hundred lines of tricky code, those niebloids materialise
// the sentinel into an iterator (`ranges::next`, O(1) for the sized ranges these
// require) and delegate to the classic algorithm through a projection-composed
// comparator/predicate. The classic calls are spelled `std::sort`, `std::…`
// (i.e. ::std::), never unqualified — an unqualified `sort` here would re-enter
// this very niebloid. partition_point / is_partitioned / partition_copy /
// partial_sort_copy carry no matching classic return shape and are direct.
#ifndef BOXCXX_BITS_RANGES_ALGO_SORT
#define BOXCXX_BITS_RANGES_ALGO_SORT

